My approach:-
1.Sort the given vector so that everything will be ordered
2.Run a outer loop and create a variable diff which calculates the diff between the element and before element
3.Inside the inner for loop from j = 1 till diff so that I can insert diff number of elements in the new vector 
4.return the new vector

Time complexity:- O(N2) in worst case
Because, if diff is such large then only we need to run the inner loop for N times so time complexity will become O(N2)
Space complexity:- O(N) in worst case 
As we are storing missing elements in the new vector

My code:-
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> findMissingElements(vector<int>& nums) {
        vector<int> vec;
        sort(nums.begin(),nums.end());
        for(int i  = 1;i<nums.size();i++){
            int diff = nums[i] - nums[i-1];
            for(int j = 1;j<diff;j++){
                vec.push_back(nums[i-1]+j);
            }
        }
        return vec;
    }
};
